.Im MicroEmacs variable|buffer|macrodevelop
.so me.tni
.TH $buffer-code-page 5
.XI $buffer-code-page - "Buffer single byte code page"
.SH NAME
.na
$buffer-code-page \- Buffer single byte code page
.Me $a
.ad
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB$buffer-code-page\fR "\fIname\fR"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B $buffer-code-page
is the name of the code page of the current buffer's file, a code page defined by
.Ht set-char-mask 2
flag \fBC\fR, normally with
.Ht code-page-define 3 .
When set the code page must exist.
.PP
A Unicode build reads a file which is not UTF-8 with the current code page, which the buffer keeps, and writes it
back with the buffer's code page, so a file stays byte identical. Setting a different code page converts the file
when next saved, an empty name makes it UTF-8.
.PP
Other builds set it to the code page current when the file was loaded, the text is not converted.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.na
.Ht set-char-mask 2 ,
.Ht code-page-define 3 ,
.Ht change-buffer-encoding 3 .
.ad
.FH
